  "narrative": {
    "intro": "North Carolina has received $174M in federal contract obligations so far in FY2027. The state has 1,469 awards with an average award size of $119K. Obligations fell 96.9% year over year. These totals are partial, fiscal year to date. Department of Agriculture leads buying with $99.5M, and Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $48.9M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC is the largest vendor with $99.6M. Logging is the largest industry by obligations with $99.6M. Other sizable industry categories include Research and Development in Biotechnology (except Nanobiotechnology) with $7.3M, Other Computer Related Services with $6.8M, and Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing with $6.4M. Recent fiscal years show larger annual totals, including FY25 at $9.3B and FY22 at $8.6B, which provides context for the current year to date total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 96.9% year over year. FY27 to date obligations are $174M compared with prior full-year totals such as FY26 at $5.7B and FY25 at $9.3B. The current-year total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure, not a full fiscal year total. That makes direct comparisons to full-year totals a context note rather than a like-for-like measure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors account for most spending?",
        "body": "Department of Agriculture obligated $99.5M, making it the top buying agency in FY2027 to date. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC received $99.6M, making it the top vendor in FY2027 to date. Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $48.9M and Department of Justice obligated $8.5M. The Logging industry accounted for $99.6M of obligations, followed by Research and Development in Biotechnology (except Nanobiotechnology) at $7.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
